From: xmrblocks security audit <security@monerofund.org>
Subject: [PATCH 0010] finding 10: stop exceptions escaping route handlers

crow does not wrap handler_->handle() in a try/catch. An exception thrown from a
route unwinds into the asio worker loop, which catches std::exception and logs
"Worker Crash" -- but res.complete_request_handler_ is never invoked, so the
response is never completed and the client's connection hangs until timeout.
Repeated triggering leaks connections and worker capacity.

Three sites:

  * construct_tx_context(): out_amount_indices.at(output_idx) throws whenever the
    DB returns fewer amount indices than the transaction has outputs. The
    existing !empty() guard does not cover that case; compare sizes instead.
  * the ring-member loop: mixin_outputs.at(count) throws when fewer outputs come
    back than there are absolute offsets. Break out of the ring rather than
    abandoning the request -- the surrounding code already handles a short ring.
  * show_ringmemberstx_hex(): threw std::runtime_error outright. Return the
    message like every other failure path in that function.

A blanket try/catch around each route body would also be reasonable defence in
depth, but these three are the reachable ones and the targeted fixes keep the
error text useful.
---
diff --git a/src/page.h b/src/page.h
index 5eed1e1..75cfec9 100644
--- a/src/page.h
+++ b/src/page.h
@@ -1623,12 +1623,18 @@ show_ringmemberstx_hex(string const& tx_hash_str)
 
            transaction mixin_tx;
 
            if (!mcore->get_tx(mixin_tx_hash, mixin_tx))
            {
-               throw std::runtime_error("Cant get tx: "
-                                        + pod_to_hex(mixin_tx_hash));
+               // Returning beats throwing: crow does not wrap handler
+               // invocation, so an escaping exception unwinds into the asio
+               // worker loop and the response is never completed.
+               string out_msg = "Cant get tx: " + pod_to_hex(mixin_tx_hash);
+
+               cerr << out_msg << endl;
+
+               return out_msg;
            }
 
            // serialize tx
            string tx_hex = epee::string_tools::buff_to_hex_nodelimer(
                                    t_serializable_object_to_blob(mixin_tx));
@@ -2412,10 +2418,17 @@ show_my_outputs(string tx_hash_str,
             // for each found output public key check if its ours or not
             for (const uint64_t& abs_offset: absolute_offsets)
             {
 
                 // get basic information about mixn's output
+                if (count >= mixin_outputs.size())
+                {
+                    cerr << "Mixin output " << count << " missing for key image "
+                         << pod_to_hex(in_key.k_image) << '\n';
+                    break;
+                }
+
                 cryptonote::output_data_t output_data = mixin_outputs.at(count);
 
                 tx_out_index tx_out_idx;
 
                 try
@@ -6579,11 +6592,11 @@ construct_tx_context(transaction tx, uint16_t with_ring_signatures = 0)
 
         string out_amount_index_str {"N/A"};
 
         // outputs in tx in them mempool dont have yet global indices
         // thus for them, we print N/A
-        if (!out_amount_indices.empty())
+        if (output_idx < out_amount_indices.size())
         {
             out_amount_index_str
                     = std::to_string(out_amount_indices.at(output_idx));
         }
 
